Note on Redis: Redis 7.4 through 7.x were dual-licensed RSALv2/SSPLv1, neither of
which is OSI-approved. From Redis 8.0 (May 2025) Redis is tri-licensed and may be
used under the GNU Affero General Public License v3, which IS OSI-approved. Qeema
therefore pins Redis >= 8.0 and elects the AGPLv3 option, satisfying the
all-OSI-dependencies requirement without substituting the component. Redis runs as
a separate, unmodified network service; AGPLv3 imposes no license obligation on
Qeema's own Apache-2.0 source. Operators preferring a permissive licence may set
REDIS_IMAGE to the wire-compatible Valkey (BSD-3-Clause) with no code changes.
See docs/adr/0002-redis-licensing.md.

Note on map tiles: Qeema ships no commercial tile provider. Location geometry is
rendered from OpenStreetMap-derived GeoJSON redistributed under the Open Database
License (ODbL) 1.0, bundled with the country configuration. Attribution is
displayed in the dashboard as ODbL requires. See docs/adr/0003-map-rendering.md.
